# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Morrow Coffee Co. — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for development (Vite loads it automatically).
# Only VITE_-prefixed variables are exposed to the browser bundle.
# NEVER put a secret in a VITE_ variable — it ships to every visitor.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Email delivery (EmailJS) ----------------------------------------------
# The three identifiers below make every form send real email to your inbox.
# While any of them is missing the app runs in DEMO MODE: submissions are
# simulated, the UI labels them as demos, and nothing is sent.
#
# See docs/EMAIL_SETUP.md for the 5-minute setup, including the exact template
# body to paste into the EmailJS dashboard.
#
# These keys are publishable by design. Protect them with the allowed-origins
# list in the EmailJS dashboard, not by hiding them.
# VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=service_abc1234
# VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=template_xyz987
# VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=dQw4w9WgXcQ...

# Where notified emails are delivered. Optional: defaults to
# alameenahmed588@gmail.com (see DEFAULT_TO_EMAIL in src/services/form.service.ts).
# Passed to the template as {{to_email}}. If your EmailJS template has a
# "To email" address set in the dashboard, THAT wins — keep the two in sync.
# VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL=alameenahmed588@gmail.com

# --- Site identity ---------------------------------------------------------
# Public origin of the deployed site, no trailing slash.
# Used for canonical URLs and absolute Open Graph / Twitter image URLs.
# Leave empty until the real domain is confirmed: the app then omits
# <link rel="canonical"> rather than pointing at a made-up host.
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://www.example.com

# Optional: analytics id (not wired up — documented so it is not invented later).
# VITE_ANALYTICS_ID=
